hat I can offer as general practice:\n\n- **Cash vs. in-kind:** Irish ETFs often set different cut-offs for the two, typically with an earlier deadline for in-kind creations and redemptions because the basket must be delivered and validated before the valuation point.\n- **Hedged vs. unhedged classes:** Share classes usually share the fund's dealing day, but hedged classes may need earlier cut-offs so that FX hedging trades can be executed and allocated.\n\nFor a definitive answer, check:\n1. The consolidated text of S.I. 352/2011 on the Irish Statute Book.\n2. The Central Bank of Ireland's UCITS Q&A and any 2026 notices.\n3. The fund's prospectus and supplement, which set the actual cut-off times.\n\nIf you can share the relevant extract, I can help you interpret it.","ttft_ms":2759,"type":"result","duration_ms":4490,"uuid":"50f9e3e1-9fc8-4236-8a68-822b47eca924","ttft_stream_ms":395,"time_to_request_ms":52,"first_content_frame_ms":395,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
